/* =====================================================================
   HOUSING TAB  —  U.S. Housing Market Index (USHMI)
   Open replication of the RecessionALERT USHMI report, built from FRED.
   Drop-in for:  macro-regime/src/tabs/HousingTab.jsx
   Matches the MACRO REGIME dark-terminal aesthetic (JetBrains Mono).

   Housing is the most cyclical, most rate-sensitive corner of the economy:
   7 of the last 11 U.S. recessions were preceded by a big decline in housing.
   The USHMI averages 8 highly cyclical housing components that turn down on
   average ~14 months before recession (6-month SD, CoV 0.42). Chronology:
   permits -> starts -> completions -> supply -> new & existing sales.
   ===================================================================== */

